1045:
(a) The following rules shall be applied to all dog parks within the City of Morrow:
(1) Dog owner/custodian is legally and financially responsible for the actions of their dog;
(2) Dog owners/custodians assume all risks associated with usage of the park;
(3) Parking is for general park/dog park users and path walkers only;
(4) A dog owner/custodian must remove any feces left by their dog within the park. Dog waste shall be immediately removed by placing said matter in a closed or sealed container and thereafter disposing of it in a trash receptacle, sanitary disposal unit or other closed or sealed refuse container;
(5) Dog waste receptacles are for dog waste only. Users of the park are prohibited from discarding other garbage/waste in the dog waste receptacles.
(6) Water stations and bowls are for dogs to drink from only. Bathing, washing, and human consumption of water is prohibited within the dog park.
(7) The following are prohibited from any city dog park:
a. Alcoholic beverages;
b. Music;
c. Pet or human food;
d. Glass containers;
e. Smoking;
f. Littering.
(8) Park hours of operation shall be between the hours of 6:00 a.m. and 8:00 p.m. No person shall use the park between the hours of 8:00 p.m. and 6:00 a.m. daily. During the winter months, park hours of operation shall be between the hours of 6:00 a.m. and 6:00 p.m. No person shall use the park between the hours of 6:00 a.m. and 6:00 p.m.
(9) No dog owner/custodian may bring more than two dogs into the park at one time;
(10) A dog owner/custodian must be 16 years of age or older to enter the park;
(11) A child between the ages of ten and 16 years may enter the dog park only with adult supervision;
(12) Children under the age of ten are prohibited from entering the dog park;
(13) Dogs that have been bred or trained for fighting purposes are prohibited;
(14) All dogs are required to wear, or the owner/custodian must carry, current vaccination and registration tags, which may be checked by the animal control authority or other law enforcement;
(15) Dogs are to be brought to the park on leashes and released inside the dog park. Upon exiting the park dogs must be under the control of a leash. Spike, choke, electric, or prong collars are prohibited in the park;
(16) No female dog in heat, or sick dog, shall be brought into the dog park;
(17) Dog owners/custodians are to remain in visual contact with their dogs in the park, and shall have verbal control of their dogs in the park;
(18) A dog owner/custodian shall immediately leash and remove a dog that becomes aggressive, regardless of whether the dog has a history of bites or has been designated as a dangerous or vicious dog under state or other applicable law; in no event may a dog that has been designated as dangerous or vicious be brought into the park. Criminal penalties apply to bringing a dangerous or vicious dog into this park;
(19) Dog bites shall be reported to the City of Morrow Police Department by anyone involved or witnessing the bite;
(20) A dog owner/custodian is responsible for destruction caused by his or her dog. Destruction shall include any hole a dog may dig while in the park;
(21) In case of danger or emergency, contact 911;
(b) Persons violating the dog park rules established herein shall be guilty of a city ordinance violation and subject to the following penalties plus court costs, if applicable:
(1) First offense: $50.00 fine;
(2) Second offense: $100.00 fine;
(3) Third offense: $250.00 and six month trespass from all city dog parks.
(Ord. No. 2019-02, § 1(Exh. A), 5-14-19)
